                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_24\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix (StatusUpdaterBolt: fixes bug and simplifies code) addresses a bug where the\n`fieldNameForRoutingKey.startsWith(\"metadata.\")` checks in `store()` (used to decide\nwhether the routing key should be written inside the metadata sub-object or as a\ntop-level field) always evaluated incorrectly, because by the time those checks ran,\n`fieldNameForRoutingKey` had already had all periods replaced with `%2E`. So a\nconfigured value like `\"metadata.hostname\"` had become `\"metadata%2E hostname\"`\n(literally `metadata%2Ehostname`) before the `startsWith(\"metadata.\")` test, which\ncould never match. The fix resolves this by capturing whether the field name started\nwith \"metadata.\" into a new boolean field (`routingFieldNameInMetadata`) BEFORE doing\nthe period-to-%2E replacement, and using that boolean in the later checks instead of\nre-testing the already-mangled string.\n\nCandidate_21 introduced the original (correct-at-the-time) logic: it added the\n`fieldNameForRoutingKey.startsWith(\"metadata.\")` checks in `store()` to decide whether\nto nest the routing key under metadata or place it as a top-level field\n(`builder.field(fieldNameForRoutingKey.substring(9), partitionKey)` vs\n`builder.field(fieldNameForRoutingKey, partitionKey)`). At that point `fieldNameForRoutingKey`\nwas not being transformed, so this logic worked correctly.\n\nCandidate_24 then added the period-replacement code in `prepare()`:\n```java\nfieldNameForRoutingKey = fieldNameForRoutingKey.replaceAll(\"\\\\.\", \"%2E\");\n```\nThis is applied unconditionally to the whole field name, including any \"metadata.\"\nprefix, immediately breaking the `startsWith(\"metadata.\")` checks added by\ncandidate_21 further down in `store()` \u2014 those checks could no longer match the now\npercent-encoded prefix. Candidate_24 is therefore the commit that introduced the\nregression: it did not account for the existing `startsWith(\"metadata.\")` logic that\ndepended on the field name still containing a literal \".\", causing the routing-key\nfield placement to silently misbehave for any \"metadata.xxx\" configuration going\nforward.\n\nCandidate_25 is the fix commit itself (its diff is identical to fix_commit_diff.txt),\nconfirming candidate_24 is the immediately preceding, bug-introducing change.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
